    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0493" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/748.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to
                            Haiti to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1165.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 3, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to state that I was
                    informed today by Secretary Léger that he had received a telegram yesterday from
                    the Haitian Consul at Monte Cristi by the way of Cape Haitien stating that the
                    Dominican revolutionists had formed a provisional government at Monte Cristi,
                    with Vásquez as President and Desiderio Arias as Vice President.</p>
                <p>Secretary Léger also stated that he regretted this very much as it was his hope
                    that both parties in Santo Domingo would come to some agreement whereby peace
                    would be restored both in Santo Domingo and on the frontier, thereby removing a
                    source of friction between the two Republics.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
